post1511743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It''s time for the daily silly question...<br /> <br /> The Banu Aquim Clan has access to the thaumaturgy rites in the the V5 corebook as well?</div> </div> </div> </div>Banu Haqim is the name. Banu <i><b>Aquim</b> </i>makes me think of a lineage of vampires with a thing for sailing, piracy and maybe turkish baths.<br /> <br /> Nothing bad or wrong with such a group per se, but sounds kind of niche not to mention not very canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T01:12:33-07:00","id":1511776,"title":"","content":"My bad... pirate vampires? Sounds good for a caribbean blood line!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T05:20:04-07:00","id":1511789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511743-question-banu-aquim-and-rites?p=1511749#post1511749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Banu Haqim is the name. Banu <i><b>Aquim</b> </i>makes me think of a lineage of vampires with a thing for sailing, piracy and maybe turkish baths.<br /> <br /> Nothing bad or wrong with such a group per se, but sounds kind of niche not to mention not very canon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like an idea for an Ottoman Lasombra coterie led by an elder from ancient Rome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T06:00:22-07:00","id":1512005,"title":"","content":"I may have another question:<br /> Banu Haquims are a &quot;branch&quot; of the Assamites, or they are the Assamites?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T07:32:16-07:00","id":1512011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511743-question-banu-aquim-and-rites?p=1512005#post1512005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have another question:<br /> Banu Haquims are a &quot;branch&quot; of the Assamites, or they are the Assamites?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Banu Haqim or Children of Haqim (or whatever regional translations of that are relevant, I suppose) is the name used by the Clan to refer to themselves.<br /> Assamite is what outsiders refer to them as. Not entirely sure, but I believe it's a corruption of Hassamite, with Hassam being one of the ways Haqim's name was mutated by word of mouth back in medieval times. So it's basically still a variant of Banu Haqim. <span style=\"font-size:10px\">(Wouldn't surprise me if Assamite was originally chosen for sounding a bit like &quot;assassin&quot; though. I mean we have Clan Johnson (but Italian!), Clan &quot;The Shadow&quot;, Clan Ravenous (Ravnos)... they just did whatever and added depth as they went.)</span><br /> <br /> EDIT: According to the wiki, the antediluvain has also been referred to as &quot;Assam,&quot; not &quot;Hassam&quot;. So yeah, Banu Haqim = Child of Haqim/Assam = Haqimite/Assamite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 05-18-2023, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T13:23:51-07:00","id":1512042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511743-question-banu-aquim-and-rites?p=1512005#post1512005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may have another question:<br /> Banu Haquims are a &quot;branch&quot; of the Assamites, or they are the Assamites?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a rebranding of there name for the new version of the VTM just like The Followers Of Set are calling themselves The Ministry now. It's another title that has been attached to them for storytelling reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T06:28:30-07:00","id":1512209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511743-question-banu-aquim-and-rites?p=1512042#post1512042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a rebranding of there name for the new version of the VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is quite an old rebranding<br /> In Veil of Night it was revealed they always called themselves the Banu Haqim, or Children of Haqim, especially in the Middle East and North Africa. Superior in numbers to the other bay't in the area, many of the Banu Haqim worked hand-in-hand with the Ashirra to keep the Europeans out, especially since the majority of the clan was Muslim. <br /> It is a 2001 suplement<br /> But even before that I think they were called in some DA sourced Banu Haqim (not sure about that part)<br /> Also, Banu is Arabic for &quot;the children of&quot; or &quot;descendants of&quot; and appears before the name of a tribal progenitor. So since the Clan was founded by Haqim, Banu Haqim was always correct technically<br /> So I wouldn't call it rebranding; the term &quot;Assamite&quot; was always a bit insulting and was a bit of a berserk button (ready to be exploited in a clever players hand). They always hated being called &quot;Assamites&quot; &quot;Assamite&quot; was the other Kindred's name for them, based on a mispronunciation of their own name for themselves. Like that &quot;N&quot; word... <br /> Anyhow, even if the term appeared first in Veil of Night... then in later suplements, more than two decade of usage of the term is not really rebranding <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-20T09:37:08-07:00","id":1512220,"title":"","content":"I do remember that from Veil of Night Shadeprowler now and it was a nice way of reminding visiting Kindred who were the kings and queens there and call them by that title. But now it's becoming more common by the neonates and younger ancilla's whom have become the big shots with most of the elders &amp; ancients gone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}